    "summary": "All fBm variants (QLIKE 14-133) are catastrophically worse than HAR-ABS (1.63) and GJR-GARCH (1.70). Cross-asset info helps WITHIN fBm class (Triv 14.7 vs Univ 132.6, DM=-2.52) but the entire fBm class is unusable for daily vol forecasting with daily proxy data. Spearman rho for fBm variants is essentially zero (0.006-0.049, all NS), vs HAR-ABS 0.167 and GJR 0.147 (both p<0.001). The HAR-like approximation with H-dependent weights does not capture enough of the fBm conditional expectation structure. Likely needs intraday RV data to be competitive.",
